Subject: [PATCH] latent-defense-mcp: sanitize filenames built from tool arguments

Backported from upstream commit a663cec00a02b8b4183aace2b85270ea3f2efce3
("Added Cursor support.") in https://github.com/latent-defense/latent-defense-mcp.

Our vendored copy stays pinned at 85917e7 because that upstream commit also
relicenses the package to Proprietary and builds its skill bundle with a forced
include from .claude/skills and .cursor/skills, which we strip when vendoring —
so the wheel no longer builds. Those questions are with the vendor. These two
fixes are not contingent on the answers, so they come across on their own.

Both bugs let an MCP tool argument steer a filesystem write out of its intended
directory:

  * energy_cache._db_path() interpolated branch_id straight into a SQLite
    filename.
  * triage_state built user- and project-profile JSON filenames from tool
    arguments unsanitised (10 call sites).

Scope: the security hunks only. The same upstream commit adds a
ticketing_integration profile field and scrubs some internal references from
comments; both are deliberately left out so this patch stays reviewable.

Drop this patch once we vendor a663cec or later — upstream carries these exact
lines, so the tree converges with no conflict.

Already applied to the vendored tree; kept here so a re-vendor can re-apply it:
    git apply third_party/patches/latent-defense-mcp/0001-*.patch

Verified: upstream's suite passes with it applied (164 tests, unchanged from the
bare pin), and a probe driving the real tool functions with a traversal payload
escapes its directory before the patch and stays contained after.

